  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nSaturday was another day of solid HI's topping out in the \n105-110 degree range, adding to our prolonged duration extreme \nheat. There were isolated higher totals up to 113 degrees, very\nsimilar to Friday. This was on target and will be so yet again \ntoday with very similar conditions to the past 2 days. Heat \nheadlines will thus remain in effect thru what will hopefully be\nits final day today.\n\nWhat changes after that is a noisier pattern manifest from\nfalling heights as the ridge shows some breaks and ultimately, a\ncouple frontal approaches and passages. The first such will be \ntonight into Monday, and there is a widespread swath of \nMarginal/Slight Risk severe with its presence, extending its entire \nlatitudinal bounds from MO-VA. Temperatures and dew points fall off \nafter passage, but may not quite or fully enough to totally preclude \nanother heat headline in our south for Monday. The dew point drop \noff stalls a little down there in its decreasing wax, as upper 70s \nstill hover on our southern borders in the late PM, before dropping \noff in the evening. Fortunately, high temps do cool back toward \nclimo near 90F. As a result, at least at this writing, we're not \nprepared to extend, but it will be something to focus upon in the \nnext 24 hours as peak HI's along our southern border flirt with \nAdvisory criteria.\n\nAnother system takes shape by mid week, and it is messier in the\nmodels with its resolution, but for all practical purposes, it\nmakes incoming approach Wednesday with passage Wednesday night\ninto Thursday. Pops will spike during this time frame and a\nsharper punch of cooler/drier air is anticipated when its\npassage is completed. While no severe storms are highlighted \nnow, we suspect this may change as the pattern metamorphosis \noccurs and the mid week nears. On the plus side is the fruit \nthat'll bear, as we're looking at dew points returning to the \n60s by week's end, with Thursday-Friday highs solidly in the \nmid-upper 80s; a spectacular end to the week weather-wise, \nparticularly in comparison to the prior week of extreme heat. \nWe'll need to enjoy it while we can as both the 6-10 and 8-14 \nday outlooks return an Above normal temperature signal.",
